 ## Data Expectations
 - Outputs/reference files should be JSON arrays. Each element may be a string or object containing `text`/`output` fields.
 - Future work: support tabular CSV, scored datasets, multi-turn conversations.
 
+## Threshold Gating for CI
+- `generateReport` accepts optional `thresholds` object mapping metric IDs to minimum scores (0–1).
+- Threshold check: score ≥ min passes; missing metrics or null scores fail.
+- Report gains top-level `passed` boolean and `thresholds` array with `{ metric, min, score, passed }` per threshold.
+- Markdown reports render a "Thresholds" section with PASS/FAIL status for each.
+- CLI exits 1 if any threshold fails (exit 0 if all pass or no thresholds supplied).
+- Unknown metric IDs or malformed thresholds (`not <metric>=<number>` or score outside 0–1) exit 2 with usage error.
+
 ## Extensibility Hooks
 - `frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js` exposes `DEFAULT_METRICS`; additional metrics can be registered by passing custom evaluators to `runEvaluations`.
 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
+- Custom metrics can be passed to `generateReport` thresholds, enabling SDK users to gate on their own metric types.
 - CLI parsing accommodates further evaluation subcommands (e.g., `frai eval bias`).
 
